IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lta-common`
IMPORT `taa-procedure`
IMPORT `lta-core`
IMPORT `lta-seat`

-- Land Tax Act 1936 (SA), with the Taxation Administration Act 1996 (SA) -- cases for the owner's seat (lta-seat.l4),
-- asked with plain answers, as the owner would give them.
--
-- Expected values worked by hand from the deposited texts (not the official texts, and out of date), never copied from
-- the encoding's output. THRESHOLDS are ASSUMED for the case (A $700 000, B $1 100 000, C $1 600 000, D $2 100 000)
-- unless the Act states them; none is a gazetted figure. Market rates are ASSUMED.

§ `Cases -- the owner of land (seat)`

§§ `When the land tax is worked out, and who pays`

#ASSERT `At midnight on which day are the facts fixed for my land tax` 2026 EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 6 30
#ASSERT `Am I liable for the land tax on this land` `legal owner` FALSE EQUALS `liable for the land tax on the land`
-- Bought under a contract not settled by 30 June: an owner as prospective owner, with the seller still the legal owner.
#ASSERT `Am I liable for the land tax on this land` `prospective owner, under a contract to purchase or acquire the land` TRUE EQUALS `liable, unless the Commissioner treats the owners in another capacity as the sole owners (s 9(2))`
#ASSERT `Am I liable for the land tax on this land` `tenant under an ordinary lease only` FALSE EQUALS `not liable: not an owner of the land at midnight on 30 June before the year`
#ASSERT `Am I still liable after selling during the year` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I still liable after selling during the year` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Can I be made to pay all the land tax on land I own with others` 2
#ASSERT `How much can I recover from my co-owners` 3501 50 EQUALS 1750.5

§§ `Is my home exempt?`

-- My home, mine alone, a study used for business on 10% of the floor area: wholly exempt.
#ASSERT `Are there proper grounds to exempt my home` TRUE TRUE FALSE 10 90 FALSE 100 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `wholly exempt under` `s 5(10)(a)`
-- I own half with my sister, who lives elsewhere: still wholly exempt ("whether or not he or she is the sole owner").
#ASSERT `Are there proper grounds to exempt my home` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 100 TRUE 50 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `wholly exempt under` `s 5(10)(a)`
-- I live there but own only 3%, and the Commissioner is not satisfied the interest was for other purposes: none.
#ASSERT `Are there proper grounds to exempt my home` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 100 TRUE 3 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no exemption on these grounds`
-- A shop-front on 40%: partly exempt, value reduced by 60%.
#ASSERT `Are there proper grounds to exempt my home` TRUE TRUE FALSE 40 60 FALSE 100 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `partially exempt under` `s 5(10)(b)` 60
-- A motel I live in, 80% of the floor area my residence: wholly exempt.
#ASSERT `Are there proper grounds to exempt my home` TRUE FALSE TRUE 20 80 FALSE 100 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `wholly exempt under` `s 5(10)(ba)`
#ASSERT `By what percentage is my home's taxable value reduced for business use` 40 EQUALS 60
#ASSERT `By what percentage is my home's taxable value reduced for business use` 76 EQUALS 0
-- Site value $800 000, 40% business, exemption granted: $320 000. Not yet granted: the full $800 000.
#ASSERT `What is the taxable value of my home after its exemption` 800000 TRUE TRUE FALSE 40 60 FALSE 100 FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS 320000
#ASSERT `What is the taxable value of my home after its exemption` 800000 TRUE TRUE FALSE 40 60 FALSE 100 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 800000
-- I live there but own only 3% with others, exemption granted: s 5AA(2) disregards my interest (the Commissioner not
-- satisfied otherwise), so no exemption runs through me and the whole $800 000 is taxable. Before this fix the question
-- skipped s 5AA and answered nil. With the Commissioner satisfied, the exemption stands: nil.
#ASSERT `What is the taxable value of my home after its exemption` 800000 TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 100 TRUE 3 FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS 800000
#ASSERT `What is the taxable value of my home after its exemption` 800000 TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 100 TRUE 3 TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS 0

§§ `Building, rebuilding or renovating`

-- Building on my vacant block; I will live there 12 months after completion; first year of the exemption.
#ASSERT `Is my land exempt while my home is destroyed, rebuilt, renovated or built` `the owner is, or will be, renovating or constructing a building on the land` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE 12 FALSE FALSE FALSE 100 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `wholly exempt under` `s 5(10)(ad)`
-- I moved in but sold after 11 months, with no good reason: not exempt.
#ASSERT `Is my land exempt while my home is destroyed, rebuilt, renovated or built` `the owner is, or will be, renovating or constructing a building on the land` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE 11 FALSE FALSE FALSE 100 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no exemption on these grounds`
-- I moved out of my home to renovate it, second year: exempt.
#ASSERT `Is my land exempt while my home is destroyed, rebuilt, renovated or built` `the owner moved out because a building on the land is being renovated or rebuilt` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE 1 FALSE 12 FALSE FALSE FALSE 100 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `wholly exempt under` `s 5(10)(ac)`
-- My home burnt down; I will rebuild within 3 years and move back: exempt.
#ASSERT `Is my land exempt while my home is destroyed, rebuilt, renovated or built` `the home was destroyed or made uninhabitable by an occurrence the owner was not responsible for, or by an accident` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE 100 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `wholly exempt under` `s 5(10)(ab)`
-- I own 3% with others and am building: s 5AA reaches (ad) too, so no exemption runs through me unless the
-- Commissioner is satisfied my interest was not created to reduce land tax. Before this fix the answer was (ad).
#ASSERT `Is my land exempt while my home is destroyed, rebuilt, renovated or built` `the owner is, or will be, renovating or constructing a building on the land` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE 12 FALSE FALSE TRUE 3 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no exemption on these grounds`
#ASSERT `Is my land exempt while my home is destroyed, rebuilt, renovated or built` `the owner is, or will be, renovating or constructing a building on the land` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE 12 FALSE FALSE TRUE 3 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `wholly exempt under` `s 5(10)(ad)`
-- My home burnt down; I own 20% with my children and the Commissioner thinks that was arranged to cut land tax: none.
#ASSERT `Is my land exempt while my home is destroyed, rebuilt, renovated or built` `the home was destroyed or made uninhabitable by an occurrence the owner was not responsible for, or by an accident` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE 20 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no exemption on these grounds`
#ASSERT `For how many months must I live there after the work is finished` EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `Can I still apply for a waiver or refund for a building year` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2024 8 1) (YearMonthDay 2027 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I still apply for a waiver or refund for a building year` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2024 8 1) (YearMonthDay 2030 1 1))

§§ `Moving home during the year`

#ASSERT `Can the land tax on my new home be waived or refunded` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the land tax on my new home be waived or refunded` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Can the land tax on my former home be waived or refunded` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- 2024/2025: all my land $1 250 000 with the new home ($400 000) counted: $3 500; without it $750. $2 750 waived.
#ASSERT `How much land tax can be waived or refunded on my home` 2025 TRUE 700000 1100000 1600000 2100000 FALSE 0 0 0 0 1250000 400000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the land tax, in dollars, is` 2750
-- The same, but some of the land on the assessment is held as trustee of a family trust: not covered.
#ASSERT `How much land tax can be waived or refunded on my home` 2025 TRUE 700000 1100000 1600000 2100000 FALSE 0 0 0 0 1250000 400000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `some of the land is owned as trustee of a trust: the Schedule 1 Part 3 scale (s 8A(1a)) and the separate assessment of trust land (ss 11, 13E) are not encoded`
-- I paid the seller $250 at settlement on 18 April 2025 for a $900 000 home: $1 000 x 73/365 = $200 refundable.
#ASSERT `How much of the land tax adjustment I paid can be refunded` 2025 TRUE 700000 1100000 1600000 2100000 FALSE 0 0 0 0 900000 250 (YearMonthDay 2025 4 18) FALSE EQUALS `the land tax, in dollars, is` 200
#ASSERT `How much of the land tax adjustment I paid can be refunded` 2025 TRUE 700000 1100000 1600000 2100000 FALSE 0 0 0 0 900000 250 (YearMonthDay 2025 4 18) TRUE EQUALS `not covered` `some of the land is owned as trustee of a trust: the Schedule 1 Part 3 scale (s 8A(1a)) and the separate assessment of trust land (ss 11, 13E) are not encoded`
#ASSERT `By what date must I apply for a s 5A refund` (YearMonthDay 2024 8 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2029 8 1

§§ `Retirement villages, relocatable home parks and special disability trusts`

#ASSERT `Is my retirement village land exempt` `a residential unit occupied under a residence contract by a natural person as principal place of residence` EQUALS `wholly exempt under` `s 5(10)(e)`
#ASSERT `Is my relocatable home park land exempt` TRUE TRUE `a site with a relocatable home owned and occupied by a natural person as principal place of residence` EQUALS `wholly exempt under` `s 5(10)(f)`
#ASSERT `Is my relocatable home park land exempt` TRUE FALSE `a site with a relocatable home owned and occupied by a natural person as principal place of residence` EQUALS `no exemption on these grounds`
#ASSERT `Is my special disability trust land exempt` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `wholly exempt under` `s 5(10)(h)`
#ASSERT `Can the land tax on my special disability trust land be waived or refunded` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2024 8 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 2 1)

§§ `How much land tax?`

#ASSERT `What are the land tax thresholds for the year` 2025 TRUE 700000 1100000 1600000 2100000 EQUALS `the thresholds for the year are` (`Thresholds` OF 700000, 1100000, 1600000, 2100000)
-- 2022/2023: Threshold D is the Act's $2 000 000, whatever is entered.
#ASSERT `What are the land tax thresholds for the year` 2023 TRUE 600000 950000 1400000 1999000 EQUALS `the thresholds for the year are` (`Thresholds` OF 600000, 950000, 1400000, 2000000)
#ASSERT `What are the land tax thresholds for the year` 2027 FALSE 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `the thresholds are not covered` `the thresholds for the assessment year were not supplied: the Commissioner publishes them by Gazette notice (s 8A(7)), and the s 8A(2a), (3) and (3b) formulas are missing from the deposited text`
#ASSERT `What are the land tax thresholds for the year` 2019 TRUE 700000 1100000 1600000 2100000 EQUALS `the thresholds are not covered` `the assessment year is before 2020/2021: Schedule 1 (inserted from 1 July 2020) has no scale for it, and the earlier scales are not in the deposited text`
#ASSERT `How much land tax is charged on this taxable value` 2025 TRUE 700000 1100000 1600000 2100000 FALSE 0 0 0 0 1250050 FALSE EQUALS `the land tax, in dollars, is` 3501
-- Land held as trustee is on the Schedule 1 Part 3 scale (s 8A(1a)): not covered, rather than the Part 2 figure.
#ASSERT `How much land tax is charged on this taxable value` 2025 TRUE 700000 1100000 1600000 2100000 FALSE 0 0 0 0 1250050 TRUE EQUALS `not covered` `some of the land is owned as trustee of a trust: the Schedule 1 Part 3 scale (s 8A(1a)) and the separate assessment of trust land (ss 11, 13E) are not encoded`
#ASSERT `How much land tax is charged on this taxable value` 2026 FALSE 0 0 0 0 FALSE 0 0 0 0 1250050 FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `the thresholds for the assessment year were not supplied: the Commissioner publishes them by Gazette notice (s 8A(7)), and the s 8A(2a), (3) and (3b) formulas are missing from the deposited text`
-- My home ($900 000, exempt) and other land of $1 250 050: $3 501.
#ASSERT `How much land tax must I pay on the land I own alone` 2025 TRUE 700000 1100000 1600000 2100000 FALSE 0 0 0 0 900000 TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 100 TRUE 1250050 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the land tax, in dollars, is` 3501
-- The home has a shop on 40% (taxable value $360 000) and other land is $650 050: aggregate $1 010 050, so $0.50 x
-- 3 101 parts = $1 550.50.
#ASSERT `How much land tax must I pay on the land I own alone` 2025 TRUE 700000 1100000 1600000 2100000 FALSE 0 0 0 0 900000 TRUE TRUE FALSE 40 60 TRUE 650050 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the land tax, in dollars, is` 1550.5
-- The same with the partial exemption not granted: aggregate $1 550 050, so $2 000 + $1.00 x 4 501 = $6 501.
#ASSERT `How much land tax must I pay on the land I own alone` 2025 TRUE 700000 1100000 1600000 2100000 FALSE 0 0 0 0 900000 TRUE TRUE FALSE 40 60 FALSE 650050 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the land tax, in dollars, is` 6501
-- 2025/2026 with a supplied rate change to $3.00 over D: other land $2 500 000, so $17 000 + $3.00 x 4 000 = $29 000.
#ASSERT `How much land tax must I pay on the land I own alone` 2026 TRUE 700000 1100000 1600000 2100000 TRUE 0.5 1 2 3 900000 TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 100 TRUE 2500000 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the land tax, in dollars, is` 29000
-- The $3 501 case, but: a rental is held as trustee of my family trust; or I am a unitholder of a unit trust whose
-- trustee has notified the Commissioner; or the other land is a build-to-rent block: each not covered.
#ASSERT `How much land tax must I pay on the land I own alone` 2025 TRUE 700000 1100000 1600000 2100000 FALSE 0 0 0 0 900000 TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 100 TRUE 1250050 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `some of the land is owned as trustee of a trust: the Schedule 1 Part 3 scale (s 8A(1a)) and the separate assessment of trust land (ss 11, 13E) are not encoded`
#ASSERT `How much land tax must I pay on the land I own alone` 2025 TRUE 700000 1100000 1600000 2100000 FALSE 0 0 0 0 900000 TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 100 TRUE 1250050 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `the owner is deemed an owner of land subject to a trust, as a beneficiary, unitholder or designated beneficiary (ss 12, 13, 13A, 13B): those provisions are not encoded`
#ASSERT `How much land tax must I pay on the land I own alone` 2025 TRUE 700000 1100000 1600000 2100000 FALSE 0 0 0 0 900000 TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 100 TRUE 1250050 FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not covered` `some of the land is a build-to-rent property: the s 7A reduction in taxable value is not encoded`

§§ `Land I own with others`

#ASSERT `How much land tax is on our joint assessment` 2025 TRUE 700000 1100000 1600000 2100000 FALSE 0 0 0 0 1250050 EQUALS `the land tax, in dollars, is` 3501
-- Half of $1 250 050 plus $500 000 of my own: $1 125 025, $2 251 before the deduction; less an assumed $1 000: $1 251.
#ASSERT `How much land tax is on my separate assessment as a co-owner` 2025 TRUE 700000 1100000 1600000 2100000 FALSE 0 0 0 0 50 1250050 500000 0 TRUE 1000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the land tax, in dollars, is` 1251
-- My half is held as trustee of a family trust (s 9(10): the trust counts in the separate assessment): not covered.
#ASSERT `How much land tax is on my separate assessment as a co-owner` 2025 TRUE 700000 1100000 1600000 2100000 FALSE 0 0 0 0 50 1250050 500000 0 TRUE 1000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `some of the land is owned as trustee of a trust: the Schedule 1 Part 3 scale (s 8A(1a)) and the separate assessment of trust land (ss 11, 13E) are not encoded`
#ASSERT `How much land tax is on my separate assessment as a co-owner` 2025 TRUE 700000 1100000 1600000 2100000 FALSE 0 0 0 0 50 1250050 500000 0 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `the s 9(8) deduction was not supplied: its formula is missing from the deposited text`
#ASSERT `What is the most my separate assessment can be` 2025 TRUE 700000 1100000 1600000 2100000 FALSE 0 0 0 0 50 1250050 500000 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the land tax, in dollars, is` 2251
#ASSERT `What is the most my separate assessment can be` 2025 TRUE 700000 1100000 1600000 2100000 FALSE 0 0 0 0 50 1250050 500000 0 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not covered` `the owner is deemed an owner of land subject to a trust, as a beneficiary, unitholder or designated beneficiary (ss 12, 13, 13A, 13B): those provisions are not encoded`

§§ `Paying, and telling the Commissioner`

-- Served 1 September 2025: pay by 1 October 2025 (30 days).
#ASSERT `By what date must I pay my land tax` (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 10 1
-- Received the exemption notice on 1 September 2025 and it is wrong: tell the Commissioner by 22 September 2025.
#ASSERT `By what date must I tell the Commissioner my exemption notice is wrong` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1) EQUALS `notify the Commissioner of the error or inaccuracy by` (YearMonthDay 2025 9 22)
#ASSERT `By what date must I tell the Commissioner my exemption notice is wrong` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1) EQUALS `no duty to notify arises`
#ASSERT `Must I tell the Commissioner my exemption should end or be reduced` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must I tell the Commissioner my exemption should end or be reduced` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for not telling the Commissioner` EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `What expiation fee applies for not telling the Commissioner` EQUALS 315
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for a false statement in my application` EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `Is my failure to inform the Commissioner a tax default` TRUE TRUE

§§ `Objecting and appealing`

-- Served 1 September 2025: object by 31 October 2025 (60 days); the Minister may allow it late until 1 September 2026.
#ASSERT `By what date must I lodge my objection` (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 10 31
#ASSERT `Until what date can the Minister allow my late objection` (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 9 1
#ASSERT `How much of the assessment can I object to` TRUE 3000 3501 EQUALS 501
#ASSERT NOT `Does my objection stop the land tax being collected`
-- Disallowed, decision served 1 December 2025, half the $3 501 paid, appealing on 30 January 2026 (the 60th day): I may
-- appeal. Only $1 000 paid and no permission: not yet.
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to the Supreme Court now` TRUE `the objection is disallowed` 0 (YearMonthDay 2025 12 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 12 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 30) FALSE 3501 1750.5 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I appeal to the Supreme Court now` TRUE `the objection is disallowed` 0 (YearMonthDay 2025 12 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 12 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 30) FALSE 3501 1000 FALSE)
-- The same on 1 March 2026, 90 days after service: the 60 days have run out (s 94(1)), so not without the Supreme
-- Court's leave (s 95); with it, yes. Before this fix the question answered yes without the leave.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I appeal to the Supreme Court now` TRUE `the objection is disallowed` 0 (YearMonthDay 2025 12 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 12 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) FALSE 3501 1750.5 FALSE)
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to the Supreme Court now` TRUE `the objection is disallowed` 0 (YearMonthDay 2025 12 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 12 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) TRUE 3501 1750.5 FALSE
-- No decision after 95 days, half paid, written notice to the Commissioner on 1 February 2026: I may appeal on
-- 15 February 2026 (14 days' notice, s 94(2)), not on 10 February, and not at all without the notice.
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to the Supreme Court now` FALSE `the objection is disallowed` 95 (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 2 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 2 15) FALSE 3501 1750.5 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I appeal to the Supreme Court now` FALSE `the objection is disallowed` 95 (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 2 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 2 10) FALSE 3501 1750.5 FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I appeal to the Supreme Court now` FALSE `the objection is disallowed` 95 (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 2 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 2 15) FALSE 3501 1750.5 FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I appeal to the Supreme Court now` TRUE `the objection is allowed in full` 0 (YearMonthDay 2025 12 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 12 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 30) FALSE 3501 3501 FALSE)
-- Decision served 1 December 2025: appeal by 30 January 2026; late, with leave, until 1 December 2026.
#ASSERT `By what date must I appeal` (YearMonthDay 2025 12 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 1 30
#ASSERT `Until what date can the Supreme Court allow my late appeal` (YearMonthDay 2025 12 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 12 1
-- Notice to the Commissioner on 1 February 2026: appeal on or after 15 February 2026.
#ASSERT `On what date at the earliest may I appeal an undecided objection` (YearMonthDay 2026 2 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 2 15

§§ `Interest and penalty tax`

-- $10 000 unpaid from 31 July to 12 October 2025 (73 days) at an assumed 4.00% market rate plus 8%: $240.
#ASSERT `How much interest is charged on my unpaid land tax` 10000 4.00 (YearMonthDay 2025 7 31) (YearMonthDay 2025 10 12) EQUALS 240
#ASSERT `How much penalty tax can I be charged` 10000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 2500
#ASSERT `How much penalty tax can I be charged` 10000 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `How much penalty tax can I be charged` 10000 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `By what date must I pay penalty tax` (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1) 30 EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 10 1
